  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 0757563d).\n\n**What changed.**\n- `crates/ui/src/main.rs` gets `#![cfg_attr(windows, windows_subsystem = \"windows\")]` (debug and release), so a double-click opens no console.\n- New `crates/ui/src/win_console.rs` (`#[cfg(windows)]` only, a few `extern \"system\"` kernel32/user32 declarations, no new dependency: windows-sys is only transitive here):\n  - `attach_parent_console`: `AttachConsole(ATTACH_PARENT_PROCESS)`; after a successful attach, each of STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE / STD_ERROR_HANDLE whose `GetStdHandle` is NULL or INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE is pointed at `CreateFileW(\"CONOUT$\")` via `SetStdHandle`. Valid handles (`> log.txt 2>&1`, pipes) are left alone. Rust's std calls `GetStdHandle` on every write (`library/std/src/sys/stdio/windows.rs`, `write` -> `get_handle`), so `std::io::stderr` (the tracing writer) picks up the new handle.\n  - With no console attached: a `MessageBoxW` from `main` when `run` returns non-zero, and a panic hook chained after the previous hook doing the same with the panic text. One box per process. The hook only formats and calls MessageBoxW (nothing that can panic).\n- Linux/macOS unchanged; the CLI binary is untouched and stays a console app. Decision: `docs/decisions/1278-windows-no-console.md`.\n- **No-console log destination:** with no console and no redirect the log is still lost; a per-user log file is follow-up #1323.\n\n**Verified (Linux).** `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean; `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (ui lib). For the Windows target (`x86_64-pc-windows-gnu`): `win_console.rs` compiles and is clippy-clean with `-D warnings` standalone (`rustc`/`clippy-driver --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu --emit=metadata`). A full `cargo check --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu -p camcraft-ui` could not run: `flecs_ecs_sys`'s C build needs `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc`, not installed here. So the `main.rs` Windows block is not compile-checked against the crate.\n\n**Not exercised. NOT run on Windows.** Please, a Windows tester, confirm the 4 cases:\n1. double-click: no console flash, app opens;\n2. launch from cmd / PowerShell / Git Bash: log appears in the terminal;\n3. `camcraft-ui.exe > log.txt 2>&1` and a pipe: the file/pipe gets the log;\n4. a forced start-up failure by double-click (e.g. `CAMCRAFT_GPU_BACKEND=bogus` set system-wide): an error message box appears.\nNo automated test can open a console or a message box.\n\nChangelog: Windows: double-clicking the app no longer opens a console window; terminal launches still log to the parent console, and a start-up failure without a console shows an error box (#1278, PR #1287)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1278\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
